<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
Builds the fixer that fixes one specific source mod onto one specific target mod
:raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

For a fixed-factory builder every key argument is ignored entirely -- matching the
pure-Python original&apos;s own &quot;this argument has no effect if ``_buildCls`` is not
``None``&quot; warning. Otherwise the four are looked up in #getBuilderArgs :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`
:raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

.. note::
   Use #buildAll when the target mod is not known up front -- which is the normal case,
   since one source mod can fix to several targets
</verbatim></para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>parser</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The parser the built fixer takes its data from <ndash/> passed straight to the <ref refid="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_ini_fix_builder_1adcd6dfb15a9abd828cc790e698dd2928" kindref="member">Factory</ref>, and may be <computeroutput>nullptr</computeroutput> </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>fromModName</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The name of the source mod (:cpp:member:<computeroutput><ref refid="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_mod_type_1ab473448c6f9febc57c430e315cb7a8f8" kindref="member">ModType::name</ref></computeroutput>) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>toModName</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The name of the target mod being fixed to </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>fromVersion</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
The game version the ``.ini`` file originates from
(:cpp:member:`IniFile::fromVersion`). ``std::nullopt`` means the latest listed
:raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

**Default**: ``std::nullopt``
</verbatim> </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>toVersion</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
The game version being fixed *to* (:cpp:member:`IniFile::toVersion`). ``std::nullopt``
means the latest listed :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

**Default**: ``std::nullopt``
</verbatim></para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
