        <detaileddescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
Builds **every** fixer for one source mod -- one per target mod it fixes to
:raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

This is the normal entry point. A source mod routinely fixes to more than one target
(``Jean`` fixes to both ``JeanCN`` and ``JeanSea``), so fixing an ``.ini`` file means
running each of those fixers, not picking one :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

The ``(fromVersion, fromModName, toVersion)`` triple is held fixed and ``toModName`` is
the axis fanned out over, via :cpp:func:`ModAssets::getAll` -- so each target mod
resolves its own best ``toVersion`` row independently, rather than one winning version
being picked across all of them :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;` :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

.. note::
   A **fixed-factory** builder has no table to fan out over, so it returns exactly one
   entry, keyed by the empty string. That keeps callers uniform without pretending the
   fixed flavour has targets it does not

.. note::
   Unlike #build this never throws for &quot;nothing matched&quot; -- an empty vector is a
   legitimate answer, and :cpp:func:`IniFile::fix` treats it as &quot;this mod type
   contributes nothing&quot;
</verbatim></para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>parser</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The parser the built fixers take their data from <ndash/> may be <computeroutput>nullptr</computeroutput> </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>fromModName</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The name of the source mod (:cpp:member:<computeroutput><ref refid="class_a_g_remap_core_1_1_mod_type_1ab473448c6f9febc57c430e315cb7a8f8" kindref="member">ModType::name</ref></computeroutput>) </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>fromVersion</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The game version the <computeroutput>.ini</computeroutput> file originates from. <bold>Default</bold>: <computeroutput>std::nullopt</computeroutput> </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>toVersion</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The game version being fixed <emphasis>to</emphasis>. <bold>Default</bold>: <computeroutput>std::nullopt</computeroutput> </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>filteredToModNames</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para><verbatim>embed:rst 
If given, only target mods whose name is in this set are built -- the
:cpp:member:`IniFile::filteredToModTypeNames` filter :raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`
:raw-html:`&lt;br /&gt;`

``std::nullopt`` (the default) means **no filtering**: every target mod the table lists
for this source is built
</verbatim></para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>One <computeroutput>(toModName, fixer)</computeroutput> pair per target mod, in no particular order </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
